  :question/problem "Source question: [WeBWorK Problem 5](https://webwork2.science.oregonstate.edu/webwork2/MTH_256_020_F2026/WebWork_4/5).\n\nFind the general solution to $y''+4y'+29y=0$. Use $c_1,c_2$ for arbitrary constants and $x$ as the independent variable. In WeBWorK enter the full equation $y=\\cdots$, typing the constants as `c1` and `c2`.\n\nEquation: $y=$ {{solution}}."
