  :question/id #uuid "cdf76ae9-8d62-5e5a-87bb-2dceda51f931"
  :question/problem "Source question: [WeBWorK Problem 7](https://webwork2.science.oregonstate.edu/webwork2/MTH_256_020_F2026/WebWork_4/7).\n\nFind $y(t)$ satisfying $49y''-42y'+73y=0$, $y(0)=3$, and $y'(0)=5$.\n\n$y(t)=$ {{solution}}."
  :question/answer-fields ["466a0d97-53c4-5e1e-9fb5-b57acf122269"]
  :question/worked-solution "The characteristic roots are $(3\\pm8i)/7$. Write $y=e^{3t/7}(A\\cos(8t/7)+B\\sin(8t/7))$. Then $A=3$ and $(3A+8B)/7=5$, giving $B=13/4$. These constants satisfy both initial conditions."
  :db/ensure :question/validate}
