  :question/id #uuid "eb309376-4836-5217-b757-f8ab890b29f3"
  :question/problem "Source question: [WeBWorK Problem 12](https://webwork2.science.oregonstate.edu/webwork2/MTH_256_020_F2026/WebWork_4/12).\n\nFind $y(t)$ satisfying $y''-2y'+y=252e^{7t}$, $y(0)=4$, and $y'(0)=9$.\n\n$y(t)=$ {{solution}}."
  :question/answer-fields ["ccf117f5-2ab5-5e13-be87-d21518228e9b"]
  :question/worked-solution "The homogeneous solution is $(A+Bt)e^t$. Trying $Ce^{7t}$ gives $(49-14+1)C=252$, so $C=7$. From $A+7=4$ get $A=-3$; from $A+B+49=9$ get $B=-37$. Substitution checks the forcing and the two initial conditions."
  :db/ensure :question/validate}
