  :question/worked-solution "Because $\\sin(3x),\\cos(3x)$ already solve the homogeneous equation, try $x(A\\cos(3x)+B\\sin(3x))$. Applying $D^2+9$ gives $-6A\\sin(3x)+6B\\cos(3x)$, hence $A=-1/6$, $B=1/6$."
