 {:db/id "e0d20620-89eb-5704-a32f-fb2d1d0136ec"
  :question/id #uuid "e0d20620-89eb-5704-a32f-fb2d1d0136ec"
  :question/problem "Source question: [WeBWorK Problem 14](https://webwork2.science.oregonstate.edu/webwork2/MTH_256_020_F2026/WebWork_4/14).\n\nFind $y(t)$ satisfying $y''+3y'=18\\sin(3t)+54\\cos(3t)$, $y(0)=3$, and $y'(0)=3$.\n\n$y(t)=$ {{solution}}."
  :question/answer-fields ["e6035ce3-162b-5f15-80ac-5813d55a5ce9"]
  :question/worked-solution "The homogeneous solution is $A+Be^{-3t}$. For $y_p=C\\cos(3t)+D\\sin(3t)$, matching cosine and sine coefficients gives $-9C+9D=54$ and $-9C-9D=18$, hence $C=-4$, $D=2$. Then $A+B-4=3$ and $-3B+6=3$, giving $B=1$ and $A=6$."
  :db/ensure :question/validate}
