  :question/id #uuid "414d7403-ea18-5cc2-87f3-adf188eab803"
  :question/problem "Source question: [WeBWorK Problem 15](https://webwork2.science.oregonstate.edu/webwork2/MTH_256_020_F2026/WebWork_4/15).\n\nFind a particular solution to $y''+36y=-24\\sin(6t)$.\n\n$y_p(t)=$ {{solution}}."
  :question/answer-fields ["f845bbe2-7db1-521a-adf9-435ad7b760a7"]
  :question/worked-solution "The forcing is resonant with the homogeneous sine/cosine solutions. Since $(D^2+36)[t\\cos(6t)]=-12\\sin(6t)$, multiplying by $2$ gives the required forcing $-24\\sin(6t)$."
